OBSOLETE -- disabled 2026-08-06, kept for provenance.

This removed the "${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/../cmake" include from
llvm's CMakeLists.txt, which was needed when buildroot built llvm from the
standalone llvm-<version>.src.tar.xz: that tarball has no sibling cmake/
directory, so the include failed.

Buildroot now builds from the llvm-project MONOREPO
(package/llvm-project/llvm, LLVM_SUBDIR = llvm).  Patches apply at the monorepo
root, so "a/CMakeLists.txt" no longer resolves -- the file is at
a/llvm/CMakeLists.txt -- which is the visible failure:

  Applying 001-fix-cmake.patch using patch:
  can't find file to patch at input line 5

Retargeting it would be wrong, not just unnecessary.  The monorepo DOES ship
cmake/ beside llvm/, so "../cmake" now resolves; and LLVM_COMMON_CMAKE_UTILS,
which this patch deletes, is still used further down the same file (for
LLVMVersion.cmake and the module search path).  Removing it would break the
build rather than fix it.

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index c5fa66390b..ad40ef0b45 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -2,10 +2,6 @@
 
 cmake_minimum_required(VERSION 3.20.0)
 
-set(LLVM_COMMON_CMAKE_UTILS ${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/../cmake)
-include(${LLVM_COMMON_CMAKE_UTILS}/Modules/CMakePolicy.cmake
-  NO_POLICY_SCOPE)
-
 # Builds with custom install names and installation rpath setups may not work
 # in the build tree. Allow these cases to use CMake's default build tree
 # behavior by setting `LLVM_NO_INSTALL_NAME_DIR_FOR_BUILD_TREE` to do this.
